            "parents": [
                "53c7c0e512e1b18083ade77bc8b2801713ffe4ad"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/17/82417/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Kevin Tung",
                "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                "username": "kevintungquanta"
            },
            "createdOn": 1754638077,
            "author": {
                "name": "Kevin Tung",
                "email": "kevin.tung@quantatw.com",
                "username": ""
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "WOuld reading and updating the firmware version change on the type of Chip? If yes, then we should have a different EM Type based on chip."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "The plan is to classify TPM devices solely by their specification version \u2014 either TPM 1.2 or TPM 2.0.\nThat\u2019s why I added TPM2Firmware to the enum in the EM schema (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/82416).\nIf support for TPM 1.2 is needed in the future, we can simply append TPM1Firmware to the same enum section."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please see my comment above."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Please see my response above."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/README.md",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Also u have tmp2 as different directory. Are u doing it to have facilitate a parallel flow if someone has a TPM1 chip? IF yes, then how much is the difference between two technologies in terms of reading version and update flow?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, the plan is to facilitate a parallel flow, so the same framework can support TPM 1.2, TPM 2.x, or even future versions like TPM 3.0.\nI\u2019m not certain about the exact differences between the technologies in terms of version reading and firmware update flows.\nThat\u2019s why the parent TPM class defines virtual getVersion() and updateFirmware() methods, allowing each derived TPM class to implement these functions according to the specific requirements of its TPM version."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 47,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "This is going to block the calling process, isn't it? \n\nI think we should use fdio as an example shown in https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/common/src/utils.cpp?r=a2eb951f7384c2b4fa494f90e78295f615c12a56#32"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 47,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Extended asyncSystem() to support returning the command output, allowing it to execute commands asynchronously without blocking the calling process."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 96,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "You are defaulting to IFX vendor. Is there no manufacturerId for IFX. If there is one then lets use that and set default vendor to Unknown in begining."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.cpp",
                    "line": 96,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.hpp",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please move this function to cpp file as its getting used there and also lets make this static by passing tpmIndex as in arg"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm2/tpm2.hpp",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm_device.hpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please look at my other comment related to TPM type, looks like u have a usecase for different handling for different TPM chips."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tpm/tpm_device.hpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. Firmware version reading and updating will be implemented in separate TPM classes for each TPM specification version."
                },
